# Event Registration Module — Implementation Plan

## 1. Existing Architecture Analysis

### What exists today

| Dimension | Current State |
|---|---|
| **Language / Runtime** | Java 21 |
| **Framework** | Spring Boot 3.4.1 |
| **ORM / Data Access** | Spring Data JPA + Hibernate (`spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`) |
| **Database** | MySQL 8.0 (via Docker, `sindhu_event_db`) |
| **DB driver(s)** | mysql-connector-java 8.0.33 (also mssql-jdbc present but not configured) |
| **Schema management** | `ddl-auto=update` — **no migration tool in use** |
| **Build tool** | Maven (with Maven Wrapper) |
| **Boilerplate reduction** | Lombok 1.18.24 |
| **Logging** | Default Spring Boot (Logback) |
| **Testing framework** | JUnit 5 + `spring-boot-starter-test` (Mockito included) |
| **Authentication / Security** | **None** — no Spring Security, no JWT, no sessions |
| **API convention** | REST, mixed paths `/api/events`, `/api/register`, `/api/register-event` |
| **Error handling** | `@ControllerAdvice` → `GlobalExceptionHandler` with `ResourceNotFoundException` |
| **Configuration** | `application.properties` — credentials hardcoded (not production-safe) |
| **Frontend** | Vanilla HTML + CSS + JS (single `index.html`, AOS animations, Google Fonts) |
| **Deployment** | Docker Compose (MySQL + Spring Boot JAR) on an external Docker network |
| **Package structure** | `com.sindhueventpay.{controllers, models, services, Repository, exceptions}` |

### Existing entities (skeletal — not production-ready)

| Entity | Fields | Issues |
|---|---|---|
| `Event` | `id`, `eventName`, `date`, `registrationFee` | Missing: `eventCode`, `maxRegistrations`, `registrationOpen`, timestamps, currency |
| `Registration` | `id`, `userId`, `eventId`, `paymentStatus`, `email` | Uses `Long` PK, no UUID, no `fullName`, `mobileNumber`, `aadhaarS3Key`, no enum for status |
| `User` | `id`, `name`, `email`, `phone` | Separate entity; can be kept but not needed for new flow |
| `Payment` | **Does not exist** | Must be created |

### Gap summary

- No Razorpay integration at all
- No AWS S3 integration
- No migration tool (must add Flyway)
- No Spring Security / CORS config
- No concurrency protection on registration counts
- No idempotency on any operation
- No structured logging / correlation IDs
- Credentials hardcoded in `application.properties`
- `ddl-auto=update` is dangerous in production

