## 6. S3 Strategy

| Concern | Approach |
|---|---|
| **Bucket visibility** | Private, block all public access |
| **Encryption** | SSE-S3 (server-side encryption, default) |
| **Object key pattern** | `events/{eventCode}/registrations/{registrationUUID}/aadhaar/document.{ext}` |
| **Upload timing** | On registration creation (before payment) — S3 key stored in registration |
| **On payment failure** | S3 object kept for configurable grace period (e.g., 7 days), then deleted via S3 lifecycle |
| **Admin access** | Pre-signed URL with 15-min expiry, only via authorized endpoint |
| **File validation** | MIME type from Apache Tika (content sniffing, not just extension), size ≤ 5 MB, allowed: `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `application/pdf` |
| **Credential management** | AWS IAM Role on EC2/ECS (preferred), fallback to env vars — never in code |
| **Logging** | Log S3 key only (never document content, never Aadhaar number) |

