## 7. Security Considerations

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Credential leakage | All secrets via env vars / AWS Secrets Manager |
| Razorpay key on frontend | Only `key_id` (public) exposed; `key_secret` server-side only |
| Payment trust | Frontend success ignored without server-side HMAC verification |
| Webhook forgery | HMAC-SHA256 verify against `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` on raw body |
| SQL injection | JPA/Hibernate parameterized queries |
| File upload abuse | Tika MIME sniff + size limit + allowed list |
| CORS | Explicit allowed origins configured — no wildcard in production |
| Sensitive data in logs | Custom log filter strips Aadhaar key prefix from logged fields |
| PII exposure | `registrationNumber` shown; internal UUID not exposed unless needed |
| Overbooking | Pessimistic lock (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`) on event row during payment confirmation |
| Duplicate registration IDs | Atomic MySQL `AUTO_INCREMENT` sequence via DB function/procedure |
| Duplicate webhooks | Idempotency check: `razorpayPaymentId` unique constraint; early-return if already CAPTURED |
| Concurrent payment success | DB `UNIQUE` constraint on `razorpay_payment_id` + `@Transactional` |

